{{also|takeout}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-take out.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|take<,,took,taken> out}}

# To [[remove]].
#* {{RQ:Belloc Lowndes Lodger|I|10|Thanks to that penny he had just spent so recklessly [on a newspaper] he would pass a happy hour, '''taken''', for once, '''out''' of his anxious, despondent, miserable self. It irritated him shrewdly to know that these moments of respite from carking care would not be shared with his poor wife, with careworn, troubled Ellen.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1962|month=October|title=Talking of Trains: Liverpool Street layout remodelled|journal=Modern Railways|page=222|text=At the same time, three sets of obsolete angle point protectors (used for slip connections), which were considered unsatisfactory, were '''taken out''' and several redundant connections removed.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=February 20, 2017|author=Paul Mason|title=Climate scepticism is a far-right badge of honour – even in sweltering Australia|work={{w|The Guardian}}|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2017/feb/20/sweltering-aussies-rightwing-climate-of-fear|passage=In France, 27% of voters are currently backing the Front National, a party determined to '''take''' the country '''out''' of the Paris accord, which it sees as “a communist project”.}}
# To [[escort]] someone on a [[date]].
#: {{ux|en|Let me '''take''' you '''out''' for dinner.}}
# {{lb|en|idiom}} To [[immobilize]] with [[force]]; to [[subdue]]; to [[incapacitate]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|title=[[w:In the Bleak Midwinter (novel)|In the Bleak Midwinter]]|author={{w|Julia Spencer-Fleming}}|genre=fiction|page=|ISBN=0312986769|passage=I don't know if he's close by. He's unarmed, though. He lost his gun when I '''took''' him '''out'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|title=The Dragon Girl: the Beginning|author=Steven Wood|genre=fiction|page=110|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=BbePAAAAQBAJ&pg=PA110|ISBN=|passage=I tore right through it and took him to the ground and knocked him out cold, "Ralph, oh your going to pay for that." he said and he started fighting me which he was good but not good enough and I '''took''' him '''out''' in no time.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|title=Tap Out|author=Sean Rodman|genre=fiction|page=56|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=YuTlCAAAQBAJ&pg=PA56|ISBN=|passage="Heard a rumor you '''took out''' Mr. Hassel." He mimes a punch.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|idiom}} To [[kill]] or [[destroy]].
#: {{ux|en|The soldiers were instructed to '''take out''' the enemy base by any means necessary.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=Two Faces Have I|author=Jeff Kaye|genre=fiction|page=414|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=8PGH3f9j44YC&pg=PA414|ISBN=|passage=Anyway, one of the snipers '''took''' him '''out'''.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|actor=William Smillie|role=Happy|title=[[w:The Dark Knight (film)|The Dark Knight]]|writers={{w|Christopher Nolan}} & {{w|Jonathan Nolan}}|publisher={{w|Warner Bros. Pictures}}, {{w|DC Comics}}, {{w|Legendary Pictures}}|date=2008 July 14|text=Boss told me when the guy was done, I should '''take''' him '''out'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|title=Two Standing|author=Brett Spencer|genre=fiction|page=84|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=5eJRAAAAQBAJ&pg=PA84|ISBN=|passage=Before he could get a shot off, Wilder '''took''' him '''out''' with two shots to the chest, just as Roderick '''took out''' the third shooter.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} To [[win]] a sporting [[event]], [[competition]], [[premiership]], etc.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[obtain]] by [[application]] by a [[legal]] or other [[official]] [[process]].
#: {{ux|en|'''take out''' a loan;&emsp; '''take out''' medical insurance;&emsp; '''take out''' a membership;&emsp; '''take out''' a patent}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 19, 2012|author=Josh Halliday|work={{w|The Guardian}}|title=Free speech haven or lawless cesspool – can the internet be civilised?|url=http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2012/apr/19/free-speech-haven-lawless-cesspool|passage=Southwark council, which '''took out''' the injunction against Matt, believes YouTube has become the "new playground" for gang members.}}

